course: dictionary
lesson: 5469
title: Large: big in size, number and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Large» usually means big. It can talk about size, like «a large house», or about number and amount, like «a large crowd». To check your meaning, swap in «big». If the sentence still makes sense, you have it.
explain: Large is also used for sizes of clothes, drinks and food. A large drink is bigger than a medium one. Its comparisons are larger and largest. «Asia is the largest continent» means it is bigger than all the others.
explain: Some phrases use large in a special way, so look at the whole phrase. «At large» means free and not caught: «The tiger is still at large.» «By and large» means mostly. These do not mean big, so do not guess from the single word.
fact: Large means big in size, or big in number or amount.
fact: «The kingdom of God is like a tiny mustard seed that grows into a large plant where birds nest.» A tiny seed can grow into a very big plant.
fact: Large has comparisons: large, larger, largest. Largest means the biggest of all.
fact: «At large» means free and not caught, and «by and large» means mostly.
exercise: «The kingdom of God is like a tiny mustard seed that grows into a large plant where birds nest.» What does large mean here? | *Big in size | Small and round | Free and not caught | Very quiet
exercise: «Asia is the largest continent.» What does largest mean? | Smallest | Loudest | *Biggest of all | Coldest
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the biggest: «Asia is the largest continent, with about 44 million square kilometres.» | kilometres | Asia | continent | *largest
exercise: «The tiger is still at large.» What does at large mean? | Sleeping in the sun | Very big and tall | Hungry for food | *Free and not caught
exercise: A cup is labelled «large». Which is true? | It is smaller than small | It is the smallest size | It is the same as small | *It is bigger than medium
exercise: Lily says «by and large» means very big. What does it really mean? | Not at all | *Mostly | Very big | Quickly
exercise: «A large crowd gathered at the park.» Which word means the same as large here? | *Big | Wet | Tiny | Quiet
test: «India and China alone hold more than a third of all people.» Does large or more show a big amount here? | Hold | Third | *More | Alone
test: «A large dark forest» is which kind of word? | *An adjective that describes the forest | A verb for a movement | A number | A name for a place
exam: Jayden says «at large» means very big. What does «at large» really mean? | *Free and not caught | Full of food | Very big and tall | Lost in the snow
